WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.034 --> 00:00:02.868
-My next guest is
a multi-platinum

00:00:02.868 --> 00:00:04.404
recording artist and performer,

00:00:04.404 --> 00:00:08.308
who has a brand-new E.P.
out right now called "Bang."

00:00:08.308 --> 00:00:10.142
Here is one of our favorites,
Rita Ora.

00:00:10.142 --> 00:00:11.177
Hey!

00:00:11.177 --> 00:00:12.679
Oh, that's what
I'm talking about.

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:15.548
Hey, bud.
-Hi! How are you?

00:00:15.548 --> 00:00:16.682
-I'm great.

00:00:16.682 --> 00:00:18.051
Thank you so much
for doing the show.

00:00:18.051 --> 00:00:19.585
I know that you're in Australia.

00:00:19.585 --> 00:00:22.422
So it's probably -- What?
Is it tomorrow?

00:00:22.422 --> 00:00:23.556
What day is it?
-It's tomorrow.

00:00:23.556 --> 00:00:24.957
Yeah, yeah.

00:00:24.957 --> 00:00:27.961
I have a black smoky eye for the
morning, just for you guys.

00:00:27.961 --> 00:00:30.996
-Oh! I love the smoky eye.
Thank you, my friend.

00:00:30.996 --> 00:00:32.698
I know you're in Australia

00:00:32.698 --> 00:00:35.568
because you're doing the
Australian "Voice."

00:00:35.568 --> 00:00:38.037
-Yeah.
-Who else do you judge with?

00:00:38.037 --> 00:00:42.642
-Keith Urban, and then we have
Guy Sebastian, who we love, yes.

00:00:42.642 --> 00:00:45.578
We love Keith.
And then we also have Jess.

00:00:45.578 --> 00:00:49.015
It's an amazing mix of different
styles and different vibes.

00:00:49.015 --> 00:00:50.817
And it's actually fantastic,

00:00:50.817 --> 00:00:52.518
because working
with Keith and everyone,

00:00:52.518 --> 00:00:55.221
it's really good to just,
like, turn the chair around.

00:00:55.221 --> 00:00:57.423
And because I'm so obsessed,
you know, with Keith growing up,

00:00:57.423 --> 00:00:58.891
loving his music so much,

00:00:58.891 --> 00:01:00.527
I just throw
everything at Keith.

00:01:00.527 --> 00:01:04.630
And I'm like this, "Hmm, Keith?"

00:01:04.630 --> 00:01:07.099
-Can you see each other
in the chairs?

00:01:07.099 --> 00:01:08.434
-Yeah, of course.

00:01:08.434 --> 00:01:10.103
Of course, but with
my accent, obviously,

00:01:10.103 --> 00:01:12.405
it's like "Keef"
instead of "Keith."

00:01:12.405 --> 00:01:15.541
-K-E-E-F. Keef.
-[ Laughing ] Yeah.

00:01:15.541 --> 00:01:17.476
-Keef.
-But it's amazing.

00:01:17.476 --> 00:01:19.879
It's amazing working in
Australia, to been honest.

00:01:19.879 --> 00:01:22.649
It's so beautiful, and it's a
blessing to be out here

00:01:22.649 --> 00:01:25.251
and just be working
with everything going on.

00:01:25.251 --> 00:01:26.819
So, yeah, I feel very lucky.
-Absolutely.

00:01:26.819 --> 00:01:28.187
You know what
I was going to ask you?

00:01:28.187 --> 00:01:32.891
Because you've obviously met
everybody in the business.

00:01:32.891 --> 00:01:35.395
Is there anyone that you've ever
been just kind of like,

00:01:35.395 --> 00:01:37.363
"Wow, that's -- Star-struck.

00:01:37.363 --> 00:01:38.464
That's one of my idols.

00:01:38.464 --> 00:01:41.133
That's like -- That's --
You can't even..."

00:01:41.133 --> 00:01:43.336
-The highlight of my life
is obviously Madonna.

00:01:43.336 --> 00:01:45.371
That's one of
the biggest idols of all time.

00:01:45.371 --> 00:01:48.575
And I did --
-The coolest.

00:01:48.575 --> 00:01:50.376
-Yeah. I had an
amazing moment with her.

00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:52.245
Very awkward,
but also very unbelievable.

00:01:52.245 --> 00:01:56.749
She really just made me
find my light.

00:01:56.749 --> 00:02:00.019
And by doing that,
we had to kneel on the floor.

00:02:00.019 --> 00:02:02.922
And I thought it was
"Like a Prayer"

00:02:02.922 --> 00:02:05.291
in real life
that was happening to me.

00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:08.427
I mean, I had to go
and breathe in the bathroom

00:02:08.427 --> 00:02:09.662
before I actually did meet her.

00:02:09.662 --> 00:02:11.597
I mean, this was earlier
in my career.

00:02:11.597 --> 00:02:14.934
And I was doing a campaign for
her, a clothing line.

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:17.670
And, so, then she,
you know, came to meet me,

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:19.572
and I loved it
and I just couldn't breathe.

00:02:19.572 --> 00:02:21.574
And then she was like,
"This is not my light.

00:02:21.574 --> 00:02:23.543
Let's get down."
I thought, "What?

00:02:23.543 --> 00:02:25.311
What's happening?"
And so we did.

00:02:25.311 --> 00:02:27.180
I said, "Whatever she says,
we're going to do."

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:29.482
-I mean, well, she's Madonna.
She's the one and only, man.

00:02:29.482 --> 00:02:31.384
-Yeah. The best.

00:02:31.384 --> 00:02:32.585
-Well, speaking of the
one and only,

00:02:32.585 --> 00:02:34.387
you are the one-and-only
Rita Ora.

00:02:34.387 --> 00:02:37.656
I want to talk about your
new E.P., "Bang."

00:02:37.656 --> 00:02:40.392
I love it. Here's the thing.
-Thank you.

00:02:40.392 --> 00:02:43.762
-I obviously cannot speak
for dance music.

00:02:43.762 --> 00:02:45.264
I'm not your audience.

00:02:45.264 --> 00:02:50.403
But it's so catchy
that you can't stop moving.

00:02:50.403 --> 00:02:52.505
-Thank you. Well, you know what?

00:02:52.505 --> 00:02:54.340
You know,
it's so, so strange

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:56.142
creating in this time, you know?

00:02:56.142 --> 00:02:59.912
And I think that's a lot
for a lot of people to handle

00:02:59.912 --> 00:03:02.915
and try and figure out what
they want to do.

00:03:02.915 --> 00:03:05.485
And so, for me, this is a
product of isolation,

00:03:05.485 --> 00:03:09.622
and I mean that
in the most freeing way.

00:03:09.622 --> 00:03:10.924
You know,
I wanted to do a project

00:03:10.924 --> 00:03:12.525
that felt like
there was no pressure,

00:03:12.525 --> 00:03:16.262
that a bunch of my mates really
can just jump on, get together.

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:18.864
We did it, actually,
all virtually, like this,

00:03:18.864 --> 00:03:20.799
a bit like this interview.

00:03:20.799 --> 00:03:25.037
Also, I actually collaborated
with an amazing producer,

00:03:25.037 --> 00:03:29.341
Imanbek, who is from Kazakhstan,
doesn't speak a word of English.

00:03:29.341 --> 00:03:31.243
So, I know
this might sound corny,

00:03:31.243 --> 00:03:32.811
but, really,
music has no language,

00:03:32.811 --> 00:03:34.914
'cause it was
proof with this E.P.

00:03:34.914 --> 00:03:36.649
We really just connected
through music.

00:03:36.649 --> 00:03:39.818
And I wanted it to feel like
a global phenomenon.

00:03:39.818 --> 00:03:42.087
So, you know, I invited
David Guetta on board

00:03:42.087 --> 00:03:44.457
and Gunna and Khea,

00:03:44.457 --> 00:03:47.059
who is an amazing rapper
from Argentina.

00:03:47.059 --> 00:03:49.028
So, really, there is
a little bit from everyone

00:03:49.028 --> 00:03:50.930
from all over the world
on this project.

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:53.932
-You call it the
"musical science project,"

00:03:53.932 --> 00:03:57.370
'cause I watched the short
you made, as well, online.

00:03:57.370 --> 00:03:58.905
-Thanks.
-Where was that shot?

00:03:58.905 --> 00:04:01.874
Because it was kind of --
It was beautiful.

00:04:01.874 --> 00:04:04.544
-I really wanted to take people
on a virtual experience,

00:04:04.544 --> 00:04:06.545
so we actually went to Bulgaria.

00:04:06.545 --> 00:04:09.248
And it was freezing.
It was a four-day shoot.

00:04:09.248 --> 00:04:12.585
And we really wanted to show
that contrast between

00:04:12.585 --> 00:04:14.186
glamour and incredible fashion

00:04:14.186 --> 00:04:17.923
and, I guess, cold, concrete
sort of architecture,

00:04:17.923 --> 00:04:20.225
and that's something that
I'm really fascinated with,

00:04:20.225 --> 00:04:22.428
'cause it shows
a sense of survival, you know?

00:04:22.428 --> 00:04:24.797
I'm so, so honored that
everybody seems to have loved

00:04:24.797 --> 00:04:26.165
this little world that
I've created.

00:04:26.165 --> 00:04:28.700
It really -- I didn't have any
expectations for it.

00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:32.138
So -- Oh, we also did a
special performance for you

00:04:32.138 --> 00:04:34.474
at the Sydney Opera House
this evening.

00:04:34.474 --> 00:04:36.242
-I mean,
that is above and beyond.

00:04:36.242 --> 00:04:39.679
Thank you so much for doing --
The Sydney Opera House.

00:04:39.679 --> 00:04:40.946
That's the best.
-I know.

00:04:40.946 --> 00:04:42.982
I thought, "I have to do
the best for Jimmy."

00:04:42.982 --> 00:04:45.184
-It's "Axel F", right,
you sample?

00:04:45.184 --> 00:04:48.021
-Yes! Wow! Yes, it is.
I know, I know.

00:04:48.021 --> 00:04:50.423
Listen, that reminds me
of my childhood.

00:04:50.423 --> 00:04:52.257
And when I was thinking
and talking about it

00:04:52.257 --> 00:04:55.694
with my production, I thought,
"Let's see what happens."

00:04:55.694 --> 00:04:56.763
And then I heard it
and I thought,

00:04:56.763 --> 00:04:58.064
"We're going to have to
just go for it."

00:04:58.064 --> 00:05:00.532
It's just so --
such a famous melody,

00:05:00.532 --> 00:05:02.100
and I was like,
"Let's just see what happens."

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:03.269
And I'm happy we did,

00:05:03.269 --> 00:05:04.770
because the response
has been really good.

00:05:04.770 --> 00:05:05.771
So it's good.

00:05:05.771 --> 00:05:07.806
It's a good, good song.
It's fun.

00:05:07.806 --> 00:05:09.709
-And it's a good timing,
it's perfect,

00:05:09.709 --> 00:05:11.744
because Eddie Murphy is doing --

00:05:11.744 --> 00:05:13.846
"Coming 2 America" is back,
the sequel.

00:05:13.846 --> 00:05:16.248
So, I mean, "Beverly Hills Cop."
-It all makes sense.

00:05:16.248 --> 00:05:19.184
-It's all making sense.
See? It's all really happening.

00:05:19.184 --> 00:05:20.686
This is really happening.

00:05:20.686 --> 00:05:24.657
-I think we're fortune-tellers.
I think we know the future.

00:05:24.657 --> 00:05:27.359
-Yeah. You definitely do,
because you're tomorrow.

00:05:27.359 --> 00:05:29.361
I'm yesterday.
-Oh, that's true!

00:05:29.361 --> 00:05:31.997
I'm in tomorrowland.

00:05:31.997 --> 00:05:33.733
-I love you, buddy. Rita Ora.
-I love you, too, buddy.

00:05:33.733 --> 00:05:37.870
-Check out her new E.P., "Bang,"
which is available right now.

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:39.405
Rita is performing
for us after the break.

00:05:39.405 --> 00:05:41.640
It is such a cool version.
You got to watch that.

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:42.742
Stick around.

00:05:42.742 --> 00:05:44.743
Rita, come back
whenever, ever, ever.

00:05:44.743 --> 00:05:47.580
-I love you so much. Thank you.
-Love you too, pal. Bye.

